WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.420
Six of them?

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.630
Eight!

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:49.130
One tank, three armored cars,
and the rest are armored trucks.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.580
Who the hell are these guys?!

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:56.790
Should we get in our ATs?

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:00.330
I want to check this out first.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.960
A new trailer!

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:22.750
We're after what's inside, you idiot!

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.790
Those soldiers've been
knockin' themselves out tryin' to get it!

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:27.710
I kinda doubt it's empty.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.830
They're rolling, Boss.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.790
Would you turn off the damned radio, Lucien?

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.330
Uh, right, Boss.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.130
Are we clear on this? I don't want any shooting.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:42.130
If possible, I want that trailer taken
without a scratch!

00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:44.540
Lucien, she said kill the radio!

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.880
Doesn't look like they're too well armed.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.460
I hope we can get 'em to just bail out of it.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.290
Let's go!

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:56.330
Planet Sunsa

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.210
Here they come!

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:37.920
An anti-AT tank.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.500
Okay, I know what they want.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:44.670
They're after the trailer,
and they're trying to force us out!

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:46.210
Then let's go!

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.750
I'll handle this by myself!

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.080
Looks like he's given up.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.000
Let's give him another push.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:22.670
An AT!

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.250
He wants to fight!

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:25.500
Lette, come back!

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.580
Can't stop now.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.330
Everyone, out of the way!

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:04.960
He's incredible!

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.750
He knows all this rig's weak points!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:18.250
Wait!

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.210
Chirico, tune to 75 MHz!

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.710
What?! They're your friends?!

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:30.080
I dunno! That's what I came to find out!

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.830
You, in the AT! Do you hear me?

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.040
Yeah, I hear you!

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:37.790
That voice... Chirico!

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.630
Yeah... Gotho?!

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:42.880
I knew it!

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.960
Man, you really dragged me
out a ways for this visit!

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.630
Where are you, old man?

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:48.170
Over your damn fool head!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.880
I finally found you! You really had me worried!

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:18.790
Captain! These ships we're fighting
are definitely Balarant.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:21.000
After how badly we damaged those two ships,

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.330
they're going to have to come back
for some revenge.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:25.290
We also took damage.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:28.130
Our combat effectiveness is down 30 percent.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:30.630
What are their positions?

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:34.210
Two battleships to stern,
three high-speed cruisers to starboard,

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.580
and around thirty-one smaller ships
scattered all over.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.040
All of them are laying outside of our firing range.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:43.040
Sir, shouldn't we abort this mission
to go after Chirico?

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:47.960
Captain, doing this in a cease-fire zone
is just too dangerous!

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.330
Queen takes Bishop.

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.630
King to Rook's flank.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.880
The battle has turned against you.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.790
I'm not dead yet.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:10.540
We're going to try one more attack against Chirico.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:14.040
Win or lose, once it's over,
we're pulling out of here.

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:17.500
Oh? Another rash decision, eh?

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:23.000
I wonder what Mr. Killy's expression would be if
he heard the condition "win or lose" used by you?

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.500
I have the right to protect my ship!

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:30.500
Besides, if it weren't for Ypsilon's constant
failures, we wouldn't be in this mess!

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.460
No, if you hadn't panicked and
fired on the Balarant...

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:36.790
...THEN we wouldn't be in this mess.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:44.130
Don't worry, sir. This time Ypsilon will kill Chirico.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.460
I wonder.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:48.080
You two just want to analyze his performance.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:51.580
You'd do anything to keep
dragging this battle out!

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:55.000
Clever man.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:08:01.130
If we don't push Ypsilon a bit more,
our situation will deteriorate, Gurran.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:04.790
In any case, shall we commence the attack?

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.420
Ah, Gurran! Excellent move!

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.710
But I won't retreat now!

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.130
It's medical data, sir.

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.080
I got it from the ship before it exploded.

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:26.080
Assuming this is Chirico's,
I want your opinion on it.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:29.130
These readings are completely abnormal!

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.290
What?

00:08:35.170 --> 00:08:40.000
These figures show dosage levels,
and these show body functions.

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:44.460
Chirico can heal three times faster
than a normal human being!

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.420
That's unnaturally fast!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.420
I've been thinking how strange that was.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.420
How can anyone be that tough? But, then...

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:53.830
How?

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.170
Man, what a mess!

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:14.710
If I'd known what kinda guy I was attacking,
I'd have been scared stiff!

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:18.880
So, they're your friends, Mr. Gotho?

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:20.750
You hang out with some tough customers!

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:26.540
Chirico, these guys collect
wrecked weapons left on the battlefield.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.880
Guess you could call them scrap dealers.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.670
Scrap dealers? That makes us sound bad!

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.880
We prefer to call ourselves
Weapons Restoration Specialists.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.540
It takes brains to collect usable parts
and assemble missiles. Right?

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.210
Well, I'd call you clients in any case!

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.040
And we're glad to have you, Pops!

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:50.960
If you didn't buy our restored stuff,
we wouldn't have any money!

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:56.380
So, I guess you can say we owe Gotho a lot!

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.790
Anyway, you're welcome to use our hideout.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:01.880
Having you guys there
would make us feel a lot safer.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:02.960
Right, Boss?

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.920
Exactly. You're pretty hot.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.250
The way you found that
anti-AT tank's weak points...

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.040
You must have been a hell of a soldier.

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:15.920
I used to be in the Melkian Army.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:17.540
And your lovely companion as well?

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:19.330
She's different.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:23.790
Might that be connected with that ship
and all the fighting lately?

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.540
Zophie, don't be so suspicious.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.830
We'll tell you the whole story later.

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:32.000
Until then, let's celebrate my finding my friends.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.580
And I've got some Ratever wine to do it with!

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.420
They're good people, despite appearances.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:50.000
How did you manage to find us?

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.000
Just a second here.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:57.380
Well, in my line of work you monitor
Balarant army comm traffic.

00:10:57.380 --> 00:11:02.380
When I heard about ATs in the cease-fire zone,
I just put two and two together.

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:06.500
Gotho here. Put Coconna and Vanilla on.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.500
They're here, too?

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:10.000
I'm taking care of them.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.830
Hi, Pops!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:15.040
You can relax now. I found them!

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:16.790
Chirico! Are you there?!

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:17.920
Yeah.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:20.080
Chirico, my man!

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:24.000
Chirico! He's alive! C'mon, lemme talk now!

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.830
Hey! Is this what I get after
all we've been through?!

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:28.500
Don't be jealous, Vanilla!

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.960
Coconna, don't get any weird ideas.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.960
The Phantom Lady's here, too.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.580
Ooh, Coconna!
You haven't met her yet, have you?

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.710
She's really pretty!

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.080
Ow! Why, you... What's the big idea?!

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:47.210
Shut up! I'll do whatever I want to!
Leave me alone!

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.750
As you can see, they haven't changed.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.750
Chirico!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:50.420
Hey there!

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.290
I've missed you, man!

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.130
You look great, you old dog!

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:58.960
And so do you, Miss Phantom.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.080
Thanks for helping us escape from Kummen.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:03.330
No problem.

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:08.330
So, where'd you two run off to?
Like a couple of newlyweds!

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:11.670
What's wrong, Coconna? Say hello to them.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:18.080
Oh, for Pete's sake!

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:20.500
Chirico, say something to her!

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.000
For crying out loud...

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:27.210
Come on, say something!

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.460
I hate to admit it, but you are pretty!

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:35.250
Hey! Coconna!

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:39.210
Great, she's in one of her moods again.

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:50.330
Chirico...

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:02.580
They denied it?

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:04.830
Well, that's what we were expecting.

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:06.540
Hmm, I see.

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:09.130
Guess we'll have to believe them.

00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:17.080
Our informal discussions with the
Gilgamesh Federal Forces are over.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:22.880
We've determined that the other unidentified
vessel which damaged two of our ships

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.790
isn't from Gilgamesh after all.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:27.580
I don't believe it! Then who are they?!

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:32.460
If they're not allies or enemies,
then why are they in the cease-fire zone?

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:34.500
Still no sign of them moving?

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:40.080
No, sir. However, the people they're pursuing
have moved one thousand miles to the north.

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:45.670
There's a nest of scrap thieves there,
so we can assume they've joined up with them.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:48.460
Prepare to scramble our forces!

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.420
We're attacking?

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:54.250
Yes. If the Gilgamesh have
made their denials official,

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:57.380
this won't become a seed of
instability between us.

00:14:57.380 --> 00:15:00.790
We have to capture that ship
and bring it back here!

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:15.670
Chirico?!

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:26.880
You were in love with Chirico, weren't you?

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:30.790
No, I... He's...

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.920
He's always been like this.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:35.290
I guess being a Red Shoulder
makes a guy hard-hearted.

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.130
A Red Shoulder?!

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:48.830
Chirico, are you leaving?

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:50.630
Sure you won't reconsider?

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.830
Oil pressure's still low.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:55.500
The number four leg valve's still closed.

00:16:03.420 --> 00:16:06.170
Chirico! You've changed.

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.830
You've always been rude,

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:15.290
but not saying anything to Coconna
after all this time?

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:18.170
She's head over heels for you.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:22.290
There wasn't a day that went by
where she didn't talk about you!

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.790
I'm not finished yet!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.170
You're acting ever weirder than you used to.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.880
Like an animal!

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:34.250
No, like a machine. A war machine!

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:37.920
A murder machine that was only born to fight!

00:16:39.130 --> 00:16:41.500
You couldn't possibly understand!

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:44.830
What, that you only fight
to protect your own skin?

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:46.750
Well, I pity you, then!

00:16:47.630 --> 00:16:51.540
You have friends,
women who love you, food to eat.

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:53.210
What more do you need?!

00:16:53.210 --> 00:16:56.580
Or maybe the normal pleasures in life
aren't enough for you.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.670
Stop it!

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.540
No wonder you've made so many enemies!

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.040
God help you if you should ever have to relax!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:06.540
Does that mask you like to wear
make you happy?

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.630
Or does it hide the fact that
you're terrified of dying?!

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:09.500
Stop it!

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:12.080
He was a Red Shoulder!

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:15.250
Nobody can ever really understand
what that means!

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:17.830
He wasn't the only one!

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:20.290
It's not just that! Chirico's-!

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:24.710
Chirico's what?

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:27.750
Well...

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:34.540
What, is he a PS or something?

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:37.460
Well, that would explain things.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.040
Fyana!

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:43.920
I'm a fool! I don't know what I'm talking about!

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:44.830
Never mind.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:07.710
ATs! Twelve...

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:08.880
No, fifteen of them!

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.540
Hey, how many cannons do we have?

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:13.290
Twenty. We just don't have enough people here!

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:16.710
Do you hear me, scrap thieves?!

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:18.000
Yeah, what?!

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.630
I know Chirico's in there!

00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:22.580
Turn him over to us and we won't attack!

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:24.250
You have ten seconds to respond!

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:27.040
We're not turning anybody over to you!

00:18:27.460 --> 00:18:28.420
Open fire!

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:41.500
Attack!

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:23.750
Now!

00:19:34.290 --> 00:19:35.710
That's the way!

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.710
The rest of you, prepare to evacuate!

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:39.330
Cease fire!

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.250
Zophie!

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:47.000
If we give them Chirico, we'll be safe!

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:48.000
What are you...?

00:19:48.380 --> 00:19:50.040
Everyone, listen to me!

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:54.750
The guy you've been fighting to protect
was a Red Shoulder!

00:19:59.040 --> 00:20:03.420
You haven't forgotten those blood sucker
Red Shoulders, have you?!

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:05.130
Like we could?!

00:20:05.130 --> 00:20:08.630
You remember what those vampires
did to our world?!

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:09.960
I'll kill him!

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:10.580
Boss!

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:12.000
Yes, Lucien.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:15.710
Your family and Lette's little sister
were killed by the Red Shoulders!

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:17.580
And Chirico was one of them!

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:32.330
Listen to me! We won't resist!

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:33.880
Cease fire!

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:35.500
You can have Chirico!

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.830
We just want Chirico and the girl.

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:48.790
You can do what you want with them! In return...

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:51.580
You have my word, we won't harm you.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:56.000
Zophie, what the hell are you doing?

00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:59.000
He's dredged up some bad memories for me.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:01.960
Vanilla!

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:05.290
Guess which little idiot
decided to open her big mouth?

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:07.750
I didn't think this would happen.

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:10.580
Zophie, aren't we friends?

00:21:10.580 --> 00:21:12.130
C'mon, do me a favor.

00:21:12.130 --> 00:21:17.460
You should know better than anyone
how much I hate the Red Shoulders.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:18.790
But...

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:23.170
I can finally get revenge for my husband
and I'm going to do just that!

00:21:27.670 --> 00:21:29.040
So much for our support.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.210
Let's go back inside.

00:21:30.210 --> 00:21:31.790
They'd just attack us.

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:32.710
But...

00:21:32.710 --> 00:21:37.080
I'll take them on. It's the only way
to buy us some time.

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:38.920
I'll help you fight!

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:39.830
No!

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:41.000
Why not?!

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.460
Look, for now I want to do this alone.

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:46.170
But what will your buying us time accomplish?!

00:21:46.170 --> 00:21:48.500
You don't trust anything or anyone!

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:49.580
Fyana...

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:53.170
Now I understand what Gotho said before.

00:21:53.170 --> 00:21:55.330
You really are alone!

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:59.290
You don't want anyone's help! Not even mine!

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:00.380
Stop it!

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:02.420
Chirico!

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:08.960
I know best how I should fight.

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:24.960
Gotho had called me a war machine.

00:22:25.540 --> 00:22:27.290
A murder machine.

00:22:28.210 --> 00:22:30.580
And now so had my beloved Fyana.

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:37.040
If I really was a machine, I doubt their words
would hurt me as much as they did.

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:43.630
But I'm just a man,
and my battle in this hell continues.

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:46.630
As does my cursed existence.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.130 --> 00:23:01.830
What now seems to have happened in a dream
is the memory of a horrible act.

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:06.460
And now, with a body permeated with
the smell of gunpowder,

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:08.880
he flees a past from which he cannot escape.

00:23:09.210 --> 00:23:11.040
Fire that still burns in his eyes.

00:23:11.040 --> 00:23:13.170
Screams that linger in his ears.

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:16.580
The moans of the red planet, Sunsa.

00:23:17.000 --> 00:23:19.000
Next time, "Deadline"

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.670
The capacity for revenge exists within everyone.

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:24.290
Deadline

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Ano hi no anata ga...
